0.01: Release tenkyu under the existing orbit app ID using the refined tenkyu implementation, reorganized settings, configurable Roman hour scale, updated sunrise/sunset rays, reduced display refresh frequency and the new 48x48 globe-and-Moon icon. Default to hidden Roman numerals, date below the Sun, time in the header and Japan / Tokyo / Chiyoda-ku. Use orbit storage/module names without importing standalone tenkyu settings.
0.02: Color the observer zenith line green by day and yellow by night; check color transitions each minute.
0.03: Add optional 30-second solar-eclipse shading: black umbra, dithered penumbra, observer above shadow; separate ephemeris/render modules with lazy tables and conservative screening.
0.04: Add a boot-owned accelerometer rest recorder, 10-second quiet confirmation, five-minute levels and a rolling 24-hour outward radial graph on the lunar orbit; configurable level-5 height (1-14 px), quiet threshold and enable switch. Preserve green daytime/yellow nighttime observer line.
0.05: Color each rest graph bar green by day and yellow by night, using the configured location and the five-minute interval end time with the observer ray's sunrise/sunset criterion.
0.06: Seven motion thresholds (0.001 g x3); configurable five-minute Z-range and periodic pulse checks hide non-wear rest bars.
0.061: Define radial rest bar height as the percent of screen-normal (Z) high-pass acceleration peaks below the 7-step threshold. Preserve non-wear HRM and Z-range checks, green daytime/yellow nighttime bars and 24-hour history; change saved history to percentage format v2 without conflating older 1-5 levels.
0.062: During a globally detected solar eclipse, show a red outline on the Moon's outer rim while preserving its original lit/dark phase rendering; restore normal colors when the eclipse ends or eclipse calculations are disabled.
0.063: Save power by locking the touchscreen when the backlight is off (preserving twist/face-up wake), caching rest-graph day/night classifications, stopping HRM immediately after a valid wear pulse, optimizing per-accelerometer-event work, and checking solar eclipses every five minutes except every 30 seconds when active. Plot the 5-minute screen-normal Z peak ratios as five outward bar lengths, stage 1 (high motion) to 5 (quiet sleep-like), with non-wear hidden; draw bars above the Moon and below the red observer marker. Add explicit missing/non-wear history markers (v3).
0.064: Replace orientation-dependent five-minute Z-axis non-wear range with a single 3D acceleration-vector drift threshold. Average X/Y/Z readings over one-second windows to reject short spikes; compare Euclidean distance from the first mean 3D vector to later means, independent of watch orientation. Retain configurable seven g-level thresholds, the separate Z-axis peak-rest calculation, HRM confirmation and stage-0 non-wear display; add orientation, tilt, motion and noise regression tests.
0.065: Fix false rest stage 5 when the watch is unworn. Track HRM outcomes as detected, absent, pending or failed; require positive pulse evidence for a worn 1–5 bar, no pulse plus 3D stillness for non-wear stage 0, and otherwise show unknown (no bar). Accept >=270 seconds of valid 3-axis coverage without the previous 2.5-second start/end constraints, correct the most recent closed bin after late HRM completion, avoid same-bin repeated HRM probes, save bounded 12-bin diagnostics and add a Last check diagnostics view in Rest graph settings.
0.066: Change rest/non-wear priority to motion-first. With >=270s valid 3-axis acceleration and drift above the configurable threshold, draw the Z-peak-based stage 1–5 bar regardless of HRM. With drift within the threshold, confirmed pulse => stage 5 and absent/failed/pending pulse => non-wear stage 0. Incomplete acceleration data remain unknown. Keep historical storage, HRM probe scheduling, 3D drift threshold settings, and Last check diagnostics unchanged.
0.067: Show immediate low-cost transition frames before expensive Calendar, Settings, Orbit and Launcher navigation, with next-tick rendering and explicit framebuffer flush; acknowledge first tap during 400 ms single/double-tap handling. Add calendar-swipe first-frame feedback and combine rapid swipes into one deferred draw, preventing touches on stale date cells. Display Orbit transition on settings exit and LCD wake while preserving the idle/backlight timeout. Add navigation sequence regression tests.
0.068: Replace the Z-axis peak-count rest percentage with 3-axis high-pass peak excess accumulation over five-minute intervals. First threshold the squared combined XYZ high-pass magnitude; only peaks above the 0.001–0.729g configurable gate are detected and square-rooted. Four user-adjustable ascending accumulated-peak boundaries (initially 0.5/2/6/18g) map activity sums into rest levels 5–1. Preserve non-wear stage 0 via independent vector drift plus HRM, 270-second minimum valid coverage, 288-bin/24-hour graph, legacy v3 display compatibility, sunrise/sunset bar colors, power behavior and responsive transitions. Add diagnostics and 12.5Hz synthetic tests; previous active-bin peak-percentage state is not reused.
0.069: Fix Place name screen not visibly opening by immediately drawing a Places... acknowledgement before deferred place-data parsing, with error reporting on failed loads. Replace the 197-country one-click-at-a-time numeric spinner with alphabetic group selection (A-D/E-H/I-L/M-P/Q-T/U-Z), initial-letter submenus and 7-country pages; add a Japan shortcut and 7-prefecture pages. Keep geographic dataset, time-zone/DST selection, manual/GPS modes, previously saved locations and all existing rest/eclipses unchanged; add location UI regression tests.
0.070: Fix the v0.069 "Places..." long freeze by making the Place name first screen truly constant-time and data-free. Replace the eager 197-country array/city parse with a compact country-name index and flash-backed orbitcities.dat with exact byte offsets; read only the selected country's city record, and the selected Japanese prefecture's municipality slice on demand. Page city and municipality lists by seven, preserve existing 197-country names/cities/coordinates, timezone/DST and stored places. Add direct data integrity and zero-index-load tests; install the new city data file in metadata. All clock, eclipse and rest behavior unchanged.
0.071: Render the existing stored non-wear value (FE/254) as thin red 1-pixel arc segments on the Moon-orbit circle, covering exactly 1.25 degrees per completed five-minute interval. Consecutive intervals join without gaps. Keep unknown/insufficient coverage (FF/255) transparent and preserve green/day-yellow/night rest stages, non-wear classification, existing history compatibility, observer layering and power management. Add regression tests for geometric alignment, adjacent 288-bin arcs, persistent non-wear and unknown data.
0.072: Display read-only tenkyu v0.072 in the settings menu title. Remove unnecessary pulse-BPM min/max settings (and stale saved keys); recognize pulse evidence only for positive finite BPM with confidence strictly above the configurable threshold. Preserve three-axis motion-first classification; suppress lone 1-second near-threshold accelerometer noise and accept motion across two consecutive 1-second averages or one >3x threshold deviation. Allow brief missing/invalid accelerometer readings without discarding a 5-minute bin when >=270s coverage remains. Skip optical HRM entirely for confirmed movement and release the orbitrest HRM power request immediately on pulse, movement, timeout or exit. Add best pulse confidence to Last check diagnostics. Preserve previously recorded v3 history and red non-wear arcs; extend device-independent power and confidence regression tests.
0.073: Make Rest graph Last check diagnostics scrollable on Bangle.js 2 and improve inspection of accelerometer and heart-rate classification.
0.074: Expand Earth-size configuration and address additional clock layout and settings issues.
0.075: Add user-selectable Roman dial numeral color, optional 5 Hz rest-graph processing mode, and reduce repeated trigonometry and wake-timer work.
0.076: Normalize the five-minute acceleration peak sum to 300 seconds when at least 270 seconds of valid XYZ coverage is available, preserving missing-data and non-wear distinctions.
0.077: Preserve a verified quiet-worn or non-worn state while the accelerometer stays still, skipping repeated HRM probes until movement or measurement gaps.
0.078: Draw the rest graph over Roman dial numerals while keeping the observer marker on top.
0.079: Display HRM measurement failures as white orbital arcs, separate from red non-wear arcs, and retry failed measurements after 1 minute then every 15 minutes.
0.080: Reuse reliable live HRM events from other applications without claiming their optical-sensor power request; keep tenkyu-owned HRM power management and show shared readings in diagnostics.
